<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">House of Pico</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Pico were an Italian noble family who ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mirandola">Mirandola</a>, north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/modena">Modena</a>, from the 14th century until 1708, first as imperial vicars and lords and later as princes and dukes. The humanist <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giovanni-pico-della-mirandola">Giovanni Pico della Mirandola</a> was a member of the family. The last duke, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francesco-maria-pico">Francesco Maria Pico</a>, lost Mirandola for siding with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-spanish-succession">War of the Spanish Succession</a>.</p></div>
